      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The problem with World Immobile is that it only \"ignores\" the positional values of the scene root, but it relies on the rotational values of the scene root. Setting it to all motion \"fixes\" the problem but then you won't have physics unless the physbone collides or is grabbed then released. Having the physics be based on parent/local offsets instead of world/scene offsets is preferred. Magica Cloth is capable of doing this with it's bone cloth scripts, and can even have the physics be based more on the animation values over moving the scene root. This would be something VRChat would have to overhaul but that could happen later for either new editions to Physbones 1.1 or have it for Physbones 1.2",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
