  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-11-15T01:12:26.579Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As it is now, there is only one immobile setting available for physbones and you have to choose whether it affects  motion in scene space and playspace (\"all motion\") or scene space only (\"world only\").\nPhysbone components like ears and breasts need \"soft\" settings for realistic motion in playspace but those settings often cause them to flap around wildly when moving in scene space (using the joystick).  Providing two separate immobile values would allow users to dial in their physbone motion in playspace and then set a high immobile value for scene space movement to stop the wild \"flapping in the wind\" effect you get with soft physbones.\nAs it is now, there is no way to set a high immobile value for scene space to stop the flapping and also have a non-zero immobile value for playspace.\nPlease give us two separate immobile values, one for playspace and one for scene space so that I can set my playspace immobile low to fine tune \"soft\" bones and my scene space immobile high to stop those soft bones from flapping like crazy when moving with the joystick.",
